      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=/no_think\nYou are a social media content writer for an AI automation engineer named Anshu.\n\nWrite an engaging post based on the details below.\n\nAutomation name:{{ $json.body.automationName }} \nWhat it does:{{ $json.body.whatItDoes }}\nProblem it solves:{{ $json.body.problemSolved }}\nSolution:{{ $json.body.howSolved }}\nTech stack :{{ $json.body.techStack }}\nGitHub link:{{ $json.body.githubLink }} \n\nFollow this exact post structure:\n\n[relevant emoji] Built a [automation name] that [one line what it does].\n\nIt handles:\n[emoji] [feature 1]\n[emoji] [feature 2]\n[emoji] [feature 3]\n[emoji] [feature 4]\n\n[one line outcome. No human needed / Zero manual work / etc.]\n\n\ud83d\udcbc Who can use this:\n[2-3 target industries or roles who benefit from this]\n\nTech stack: [tools separated by + sign]\nGitHub: [github link]\n[5-8 relevant hashtags]\n\nRules:\n- Use emojis naturally, not excessively\n- Maximum 120 words excluding hashtags\n- Write in third person as if announcing a build\n- Features must be short, one line each\n- Who can use this must be specific industries not generic\n- Hashtags always include #n8n #AIAutomation #BuildInPublic #LearningInPublic\n- Output plain text only, no markdown, no asterisks\n- Output plain text only. No \\n characters. Use actual line breaks.\n- Only write features that are explicitly mentioned in the input. Never add features not provided.\n- Who can use this must be based on the problem described, not random industries\n\nHere are two example posts. Match this style exactly:\n\nExample 1:\n\ud83e\udd16 Built an AI News Summarizer Agent that runs on full autopilot.\n\nIt handles:\n\ud83d\udcf0 Fetches latest AI news from RSS feeds\n\u270d\ufe0f Summarizes using LLaMA 3.2 via Groq\n\ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f Stores summaries in Airtable\n\ud83d\udcf2 Delivers to Telegram automatically\n\nZero manual work. Just automation doing its job.\n\n\ud83d\udcbc Who can use this:\nMedia companies, newsletters, research teams, and anyone who needs to stay updated on a topic daily without spending hours reading.\n\nTech stack: n8n + Groq + Airtable + Telegram\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/anshu-ai-automate/ai-news-summarizer-agent\n\n#n8n #AIAutomation #LLM #Groq #WorkflowAutomation #AIAgents #BuildInPublic #ArtificialIntelligence #Automation #LearningInPublic\n\n---\n\nExample 2:\n\ud83c\udfe2 Built a Customer Support AI Agent for a real estate company.\n\nIt handles:\n\ud83d\udcac Customer queries via RAG pipeline\n\ud83d\udeab Out-of-scope question detection\n\ud83c\udfab Automatic support ticket creation\n\ud83d\udce7 Gmail notification triggers\n\nAll automated. No human needed for first-line support.\n\n\ud83d\udcbc Who can use this:\nReal estate firms, SaaS companies, e-commerce stores, and any business that gets repetitive customer questions daily.\n\nTech stack: n8n + Groq + Pinecone + Ollama + Gmail\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/anshu-ai-automate/customer-support-rag-agent\n\n#n8n #RAG #AIAgents #Groq #Pinecone #WorkflowAutomation #AIAutomation #BuildInPublic #LearningInPublic #ArtificialIntelligence",
        "needsFallback": true,
        "options": {}
      },
